{"parentUuid":"1361d5ca-89e6-4f6b-b1db-9cf4ec7c2b7f","isSidechain":false,"type":"assistant","uuid":"235b7f39-ffe1-4972-8810-62e8193e4863","timestamp":"2026-11-09T10:00:03.175Z","cwd":"/Users/me/Projects/scratch","version":"2.1.319","gitBranch":"main","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# The Keeper of Halden Rock\n\nThe light at Halden Rock had been burning for ninety-one years when Ingrid Solberg took over the tending of it from her father, who had taken it over from his. Nobody on the mainland thought much about the lamp anymore. Ships had radar now, and satellites, and a dozen automated beacons that blinked across the water without anyone needing to climb the stairs. The Maritime Authority had sent letters, politely at first and then less politely, suggesting the station be decommissioned and the tower left to the gulls.\n\nIngrid had read every letter and filed them in a biscuit tin under the kitchen sink.\n\nShe was forty-three. She had come back to the island the winter her mother died, meaning to stay a month. That had been six years"}],"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgsXudYRD7PpGJY3861xo","stop_reason":null},"sessionId":"rec-stop"}
